    slug: 'david-copperfield',
    intro: "Charles Dickens's David Copperfield (1849–50) was his own favorite among his novels — the most autobiographical of his works, in which he transformed the shame and trauma of his childhood (the blacking factory, the Marshalsea, the difficult mother) into the story of David Copperfield's rise from orphan to celebrated author. The novel that established Dickens's place in the English literary pantheon and the work that Leo Tolstoy, who wept reading it, said showed what fiction at its greatest could do.",
    startWith: 'David Copperfield',
