    slug: 'barnaby-rudge',
    intro: "Charles Dickens's Barnaby Rudge (1841) is his first historical novel — set during the anti-Catholic Gordon Riots of 1780, in which London mobs burned Catholic chapels and Newgate Prison while the government was paralyzed. The novel's portrait of crowd violence and political demagoguery remained one of the most vivid fictional treatments of collective mob behavior until Gustave Le Bon's sociological account four decades later, and the scenes of Newgate Prison burning are among the most cinematically powerful Dickens ever wrote.",
