    intro: "Charles Dickens's Little Dorrit (1855–57) is set partly in the Marshalsea debtors' prison where Dickens's own father was imprisoned when Dickens was twelve — the biographical wound that marked all his fiction. The story of Amy Dorrit, who has grown up in the Marshalsea caring for her imprisoned father, and Arthur Clennam, who returns from twenty years in China to find himself implicated in a mystery his family has suppressed, is Dickens's most sustained attack on government bureaucracy and the financial speculation that was restructuring Victorian society.",
