    intro: "Thomas Hardy's The Return of the Native (1878) is set on the wild and ancient Egdon Heath — Hardy's most famous landscape, 'a place perfectly accordant with man's nature,' as he describes it at the novel's opening. The story of Eustacia Vye, who wants to escape the heath and reach Paris; Clym Yeobright, the native who returns from Paris to teach; and Damon Wildeve, the innkeeper who loves the wrong woman, is Hardy's most architecturally perfect novel and the fullest expression of his tragic vision of human desire in conflict with circumstance.",
