    slug: 'daniel-deronda',
    intro: "George Eliot's Daniel Deronda (1876) is her final and most ambitious novel — simultaneously a brilliant portrait of English upper-class society through the story of Gwendolen Harleth (one of the most psychologically complex female protagonists in Victorian fiction) and a visionary argument for Jewish self-determination through the story of Daniel Deronda himself, who discovers his Jewish identity and dedicates himself to the nascent Zionist movement. The most politically daring of Eliot's novels and the one that most divides its readers.",
    startWith: 'Middlemarch',
