    intro: "Charles Dickens's Bleak House (1852–53) is his most ambitious and technically innovative novel — an encyclopedic portrait of English society organized around the interminable Chancery lawsuit Jarndyce v Jarndyce, which has consumed the fortunes and lives of those connected to it for generations. Told partly in first-person by the orphan Esther Summerson and partly by an omniscient narrator in vivid present tense, Bleak House is considered by many critics the greatest English novel of the 19th century.",
