    intro: "Charlotte Brontë's Villette (1853) is widely considered her finest novel, though it is less frequently read than Jane Eyre — a deeply psychological, partly autobiographical work about Lucy Snowe, an Englishwoman who takes a teaching position in a Belgian school in the fictional city of Villette (based on Brussels), where she falls in love with the volatile professor Paul Emanuel. The novel is more formally experimental than Jane Eyre, more psychologically complex, and more ambiguous in its ending.",
