    intro: "Anne Brontë's The Tenant of Wildfell Hall (1848) is one of the most radical English novels of the 19th century — the story of Helen Graham, a mysterious woman who rents a nearby hall and whose diary, revealed gradually to the narrator Gilbert Markham, describes her escape from her abusive and alcoholic husband Arthur Huntingdon. The novel was the first English novel to argue explicitly for a woman's right to leave her husband, and was immediately controversial.",
