    intro: "Charles Dickens's Oliver Twist (1837–39) is the second novel by Dickens and the one that established his reputation as a social reformer as well as a storyteller — the story of the orphan Oliver, born in a workhouse and drawn into a London criminal gang led by the master criminal Fagin, that was the first English novel to take a child as its protagonist and to address directly the conditions of the urban poor and the New Poor Law of 1834.",
