    intro: "Homer's Iliad (c. 8th century BCE) is the foundational epic of Western literature — a poem about approximately 52 days in the tenth year of the Trojan War, centered on the wrath of the Greek hero Achilles after he is dishonored by the commander Agamemnon, culminating in the death of Hector, Troy's greatest defender. The Iliad explores war's cost, the nature of heroic glory, and the impossibility of mourning across enemy lines.",
