    slug: 'the-lone-ranger-and-tonto-fistfight-in-heaven',
    intro: "Sherman Alexie's The Lone Ranger and Tonto Fistfight in Heaven (1993) is a debut collection of twenty-two interconnected stories set on and around the Spokane Indian Reservation in Washington State, introducing the characters Victor Joseph and Thomas Builds-the-Fire and establishing the reservation, its basketball courts, its poverty, and its humor as the most distinctive fictional territory in contemporary Native American literature. The collection later served as the basis for Alexie's Academy Award-winning screenplay for the film Smoke Signals (1998).",
