    intro: "Carmen Maria Machado's In the Dream House (2019) is a memoir about an abusive relationship with a woman, told through the genre conventions of folklore, horror, the romance novel, the choose-your-own-adventure, and the haunted house — each chapter using a different genre's logic to approach the experience from a different angle. A landmark of contemporary memoir for both its formal invention and its exploration of an aspect of domestic violence that is systematically underrepresented in both the literature and the legal framework around abuse.",
