    intro: "Leslie Marmon Silko's Ceremony (1977) is a debut novel following Tayo, a half-Laguna Pueblo veteran who returns from the Second World War shattered by what he has witnessed and unable to re-enter the world of the Laguna pueblo, and his long healing through traditional Laguna ceremony and the help of a medicine man named Betonie. The foundational novel of the Native American literary renaissance.",
